/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  THE CASE THAT MUST NOT RUN -- and the theorem it is made of.

  Four salts on four ion families:

              KCl  K2SO4  NaCl  Na2SO4
      K     [  1     2      0      0   ]
      Na    [  0     0      1      2   ]      m = A n
      Cl    [  1     0      1      0   ]
      SO4   [  0     1      0      1   ]

  Four columns, and the RANK IS 3.  The fourth column is a combination of the
  other three -- and it must be, because the four salts are not four
  independent substances in solution.  Dissolve them and what exists is K+,
  Na+, Cl-, SO4-2 and nothing else; the LABELS "KCl" and "Na2SO4" stopped
  meaning anything the moment the crystal came apart.

  The deficiency is not an accident of these four choices.  With c cations
  and a anions the salt-basis representation has exactly

      (c - 1)(a - 1)   degrees of freedom

  and here (2-1)(2-1) = 1.  Concretely: take one mole each away from KCl and
  Na2SO4 and add one each to NaCl and K2SO4.  Every ion total is unchanged.
  Two different answers on the component basis, one identical solution.

  So the engine REFUSES.  Not because it cannot compute -- the forward map
  m = A n is perfectly well defined and the flash would converge happily --
  but because every report that NAMES components would then be silently
  picking one of infinitely many labellings and presenting it as the answer.

  THE PHYSICS IS UNAFFECTED.  Elements and charge cross the boundary either
  way, and the next unit re-speciates from the ion totals.  It is the LABELS
  that are a choice, and a choice must be declared.  Declaring it -- the
  projection convention -- is a named, separate slice; until it exists, this
  case stops here rather than guessing.

  Compare flash14_calcite_carbonate_basis, whose matrix is also not 1:1 but
  IS full rank: there the reading back is unique and no convention is needed.
  Rank, not the presence of salts, is what decides.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components    ( K2SO4  KCl  Na2SO4  NaCl  water );

equilibrium
{
    formulation electrolyteGammaPhi;

    aqueous
    {
        activityModel { model davies; }
        speciation    { masters ( Cl  K  Na  SO4 ); }
    }

    vapour    { fugacityModel idealGas; }

    volatiles ( water );
}
